9 #edb/ref 1065 3204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121039 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3d284a1f-e3a9-5b48-97e4-d621a81b5237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121039 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121063 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's again consider the following matrix:\n\n![](images/8f/8fa69630c71d5106ed04a5281681992687174891b1c0978521c12e914cb3a0b0.svg)\n\nTo find an expression for the null space using set-builder notation, we need to find all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Let's start by considering the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ and finding its reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,0] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st column). The second column is not a pivot column.\n\nNow, we convert the reduced matrix back into a system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $\\color{blue}x_1$ is a basic variable (it corresponds to the pivot column), while $\\color{red}x_2$ is a free variable (it corresponds to the non-pivot column). Because there is a free variable, the system $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has infinitely many solutions. \n\nFrom the first equation we get ${\\color{blue}x_1}=-3{\\color{red}x_2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is\n![](images/8c/8c5541adb07cb58136d71fb4e3218981f1717b929f22acbe55d133cd0c395870.svg)\n\n**Note:** It is not necessary to consider the full augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{0}]$ since the last column won't be changed during the process of reduction. Really, we just need to find the reduced row echelon form of the matrix $A$ and then set up the corresponding system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121063 #edb/ref 1065 3943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121063 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "895e6e15-cec9-50e1-9bed-dff731650d72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121063 #edb/ref 1067 "Writing the Null Space using Set-Builder Notation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245478 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245478 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245478 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8444e8ba-c379-5ef0-962e-f9d3045ba621" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245916 #edb/ref 1080 "-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245916 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245916 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b41037e1-6cef-58fa-beb9-77fb072e4a54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245997 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245997 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186245997 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bcd02285-f046-5ef2-bc6a-5641e47bade5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246041 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246041 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246041 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c1b65297-ae0b-506f-9fdb-2295eade2da9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246078 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246078 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246078 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c711b889-46b6-59bf-970c-71a8d8049a7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186245997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186246078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186245478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186246622 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2e10cd01-df1b-5da5-9789-385a9c2f8dac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247206 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247206 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111106" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247206 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247206 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -12 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2k \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247206 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "91993936-f250-5744-8e70-dfa072854477" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247206 #edb/ref 1074 "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -12 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2k \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2k-4 \\\\ 8k+16\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2k-4=0 \\\\ 8k+16=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316831 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7741c95a-c056-57b4-9397-7a01a1ba8764" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317454 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317454 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34392" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317454 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317454 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317454 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "870e5cfd-95f3-5e52-b251-41fd48145e5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317454 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428402 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428402 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the